## twitch-ad-blocker / tr — score 0.4994

**Original EN answer:**

No — Twitch ads cannot be reliably blocked by a browser extension, because Twitch inserts them into the live video stream itself, server-side. There is no separate ad request to intercept; blockers that try usually cause the well-known purple screen or stream quality drops instead.

**Back-translation:**

No—Twitch ads cannot be reliably blocked by a browser extension, as Twitch inserts them directly into the live video stream on the server side. There is no separate ad request that can be intercepted for blocking; attempts to block them often result in well-known issues such as a black screen or degraded stream quality.

